views.weakest_link:
Steps (4) and (5). The architecture would be cheap to finish only if the left image had a uniform window: a black cell in every block of length B(V), whatever the depth. Such a window can be certified once, as stripe absorption was.

The experiment shows there is no such window. For every non-ether right half tried, Ψ(R) is statistically random:
- density 0.5002 at depths 2^14 to 2^15;
- the longest zero run of Ψ(∅) is 5, 8, 10 and 12 up to depths 2^9, 2^10, 2^12 and 2^15;
- 8 of 9 fixed right halves grow by at least 3 between depths 2^9 and 2^15;
- across all 8192 right halves of width ≤ 13, the longest zero run per depth band grows from 12 in [32,64) to 23 in [1024,2048). That matches log2(number of rows × band length), the value for a random row.

So (4) needs a log W term and is a pseudorandomness theorem about specific deterministic rows. No method for it exists. It is the positive-entropy wall where every project stopped, now posed separately for each right half.

The weakest link is uniform delay against adversarial content. The reduction needs one B such that every content to the right of the first deviation leads to entry within B steps. The evidence so far:
- white or random junk after an ether prefix: at most 342 steps (this run);
- random supports: at most 134 here, and at most 829 over 1.2 million true right halves in round 2;
- round-2 adversarial hill-climbing: about 380–1070 steps.

Two kinds of adversary are untested and are the most dangerous:
- a single defect inside the aligned ether;
- a domain wall between aligned and misaligned ether.

If either heals back to pure ether, or forms a stable interface that is not one of the 109 wall states, then delays grow with distance and Absorption has a lasso, just as CQ01 does. A stable non-W109 interface inside a finite configuration could even make Absorption(0111) false.

The second risk is size. At B ≈ 350 a bulk case has about 700 free bits and about 2.5·10^5 cell variables, and the boundary layer (k ≤ 2B+13) adds several hundred instances. Chaotic dynamics may make UNSAT proofs exponentially long, and kernel-only LRAT replay at that scale does not exist yet.

ranking.assessment:
This is the only open reduction not barred by a lasso, and my run found no right half that never enters:
- all 16,426 structured contents entered (shifted-ether domain walls, short defects, white gaps, periodic backgrounds of period ≤ 8), and so did all 1,792 random bulk contents;
- the 7 slowest entered at t = 401–467;
- a steering beam did worse than random sampling, so distant cells do not seem to steer the chaotic front.

The proposed SAT endgame is out of reach, though:
- I found certified bulk counterexamples to AbsorptionWithin(400);
- the archive's boundary-layer delay of 829 already forces B ≥ 829, which means ≥ 1,671 free bits and about 10^6 cells per case;
- the delay tail looks exponential (mean 60–67 steps), with no cut-off.

The next cheap test is a moving-frame relaxation around the first deviation: if no right input at some width keeps the front free of walls, the bulk becomes a finite certificate.

Odds: tail 0111 excluded within 12 months ≈ 3%, of which by SAT < 1%. Least period 4 ≈ 1%. No effect on period 2.

Park it. The re-run confirms three things:
- the Cartier closure is lattice subsampling (0 mismatches on a random array);
- the rule-54/90/150/210 controls have mirror-symmetric orbits, so they cannot test any chirality-aware invariant;
- the natural invariant I* holds for rule 110 (117 of 128 windows), whose centre is constant.

The surviving left-permutive bridge is equivalent to the target, so S4's Lean step would formalize a tautology. < 0.5%.

judge.kill_criterion:
Drop the sideways-gap statement at once in either case:
- a computed G(V) exceeds 8 for some V ≤ 20 and W ≤ 2^15;
- some R ⊆ [1,20] has Psi R white on a whole window [W, 2W] with W ≥ 64.
Either result makes both the strong form and the [W, 2W] form false at sizes we can compute.

Stop treating CQ01 as an active attack after a 4-week time box if steps 2–3 find no structure a proof could use. Concretely, all three of these hold:
- N_g(W,V) is within noise of the random-row prediction for every V ≤ 20;
- R ↦ u(R) has no permutive or near-injective coordinate;
- the 2-kernel of Psi(∅) grows like 2^k.

In that case keep CQ01 only as the posed core, with its Lean reduction and lasso barrier, and move the effort to the moving-frame front analysis of Absorption(0111) and to the census.
